 "notes": [
  "CBSE does not publish its own Classes 1-5 mathematics syllabus; CBSE schools follow the NCERT textbooks. The 2026-27 prescription was confirmed via official government split-up syllabi (Delhi Directorate of Education; KVS where available) and the NCERT reprint 2026-27 label.",
  "NCERT's 'Learning Outcomes at the Elementary Stage' (tilops101.pdf) could not be opened (robots-blocked); outcomes are written in my own words from the chapter content and the official DoE/KVS split-up outcomes.",
  "Outcomes are not copied from the textbook; questionTypes and difficulty are my judgement.",
  "Textbook is a single annual volume; CBSE has no term split for these books, so term is null. School split-ups (DoE Delhi) divide chapters across mid-term and annual exams, which varies by school.",
  "Chapter titles are verified against two official government 2026-27 split-up syllabi (DoE Delhi; KVS HQ) and a KV school split-up, all consistent; NCERT's own contents page could not be opened. Minor variants: DoE prints 'Vacation with My Nani-Maa' and 'Fun at class party!'; KVS prints 'House of Hundreds 1/2' and 'Raksha Bandhan Revision'. Titles recorded in their most common form; exact punctuation/capitalisation as printed in the book is unverified.",
  "Chapter 7 'Raksha Bandhan' is described by DoE as a revision chapter on the four operations.",
  "Edition: first-edition year (believed 2024) unverified.",
  "Section lists are [] for this grade: NCERT chapter PDFs for this book returned robots-blocked errors to the fetch tool, and no other official source lists sub-sections. Nothing was invented."
 ],
